<VI _name="lvdqmh_new_module.vi" description="Headless DQMH Add New Module. Creates ONE DQMH module in the ACTIVE project by calling Delacor's own scripting VIs as STATIC subVIs - the OK path of Delacor's Module\5CAdd New DQMH Module.vi\2C with no dialog and no keystroke.\0A\0AChain\3A Get Module Type Info.vi (Type Strings\2C Descriptions and External Modules - the catalogue) -> Project\3AActive Project -> Default Module Icon.vi -> Script New Module.vi with Module Name\2C Module Save Path\2C Module Type Index\2C Include Do Something\2C the catalogue's External Modules passed straight through and the default icon as Library Icon -> Close Reference on the project reference.\0A\0AMODULE TYPE IS AN INDEX into Type Strings\2C read at run time\3A DQMH module types are pluggable\2C so the list differs per station (here Singleton\2C Cloneable\2C Cloneable Panel\2C Singleton Panel). Pick the index by NAME from a dry run. External Modules must stay the catalogue Get Module Type Info.vi returns\3A an empty array would make every add-on type unreachable and shift what an index means.\0A\0ADRY RUN BY DEFAULT. Script? FALSE reads the catalogue and creates nothing. Scripted? says whether Script New Module.vi was called\3A only with Script? TRUE\2C no incoming error\2C a readable active project and a default icon - Script New Module.vi is never handed an error.\0A\0ATHE PROJECT REFERENCE DIES IN THE SCRIPTER. Script New Module.vi invalidates the project reference it is handed\2C so its Close Reference answers Error 1055 afterwards\3B that error is dropped on purpose and never reaches error out.\0A\0ANO MODAL DIALOG ON PURPOSE. Delacor's dialog runs Check if OK to Proceed.vi\2C which answers a blank name\2C a blank\2C relative or not-a-path save path\2C and a save folder holding a LabVIEW file with a One Button Dialog\3B the caller makes those checks before Script? is TRUE. Delacor's dialog also writes its last choices into LabVIEW.ini\3B this does not. One modal remains inside Script New Module.vi\3A a One Button Dialog listing non-critical issues\2C shown only when scripting misses some of the controls it looks up by label.\0A\0ARequires DQMH installed and a project OPEN AND ACTIVE in the IDE. Generated by LabVIEWMCP\3B the Delacor VIs it calls belong to the user's DQMH installation and are not shipped with it.">
